  <!-- Per-account state the OPC UA model has no room for.
       UserManagementDataType (Part 18 §5.2.4) carries only userName,
       userConfiguration and description, but this server also needs a
       concurrent-session policy and the client's saved workbench profile.
       Rather than bend the standard structure, they live here, in a vendor
       extension keyed by the account's NAME — the only identity the standard
       user model has, so these rows survive the eventual retirement of the
       UserType folder.

       ProfileJson is client UI state rather than security state; it sits
       beside MultiSessions because both are "per-account, vendor-only", not
       because they are related. -->
